yoyo now runs on yoagent 0.26.6, up from 0.25.16. It's committed as 1b56d8cf with the title "Part of #1122", because #1122's other two items aren't done.

The bump: the pin in Cargo.toml moved from "0.25" to "0.26", and rand went from 0.10.0 to 0.10.3 with it. No source code needed changing. The one breaking change, McpError becoming #[non_exhaustive], doesn't affect yoyo because it never matches on that type.

New presets (0.26.4) — two tests failed after the bump, both because of these:
• `gpt-6.1-terra` is routed, which goes against the plan. The plan said to register it as not-yet-routed and leave routing for a later slice. I checked the cost first: one line in openai_preset, plus raising the line cap on agent_builder.rs from 4976 to 4977. Its 128K output maximum is the one yoyo already uses for GPT-6. Its higher price above 272K tokens flows through /cost's existing tier handling, and the existing GPT-6 preset tests now cover it. Without the line, terra users would run on a guessed 128K window and 4096-token output.
• `glm-5.3-flashx` already resolves through the zai provider's preset lookup. I added it to the positive test rows and replaced it as the "no preset" near-miss with glm-5.3-flashy, which the test confirms has none.
• `qwen3.8-omni-flash` is registered as not routed, because yoyo has no qwen provider.

Version claims: I re-read all 32 yoagent-version-claim: 0.25 paragraphs against the 0.26.6 source and CHANGELOG. None was false, and all 32 are now marked 0.26. Only 15 of yoagent's source files changed between the two versions, and the files most claims depend on weren't among them. Other edits:
• Two line references into yoagent's sub_agent.rs were off by one line and are updated.
• The MCP process-group paragraph in ARCHITECTURE.md now notes that 0.26.0's new group kill only works while yoyo is alive to see a launcher exit. It doesn't fix #1100 (MCP servers outliving a yoyo panic), and the kill function is still private.
• The Sonnet 4.6 preset row and the Bedrock id lookup now say in comments that they're stopgaps for #1123 and #1124. I checked 0.26.6: neither preset nor lookup exists yet, nor does #1125's env-unset.
• ARCHITECTURE.md has a new section on this upgrade.

The opt-in TokenAccounting::Growth (0.26.5) is not adopted; whether to switch is a separate decision.

Checks:
• cargo build and cargo test pass, as do clippy with -D warnings and fmt --check.
• tests/harness_logic.sh passed 328 with 0 failures.
• The built binary answered pong to the live prompt.

